<%- include('partials/header') %>
<div class="page-head">
  <h1>My first week, and the weeks after</h1>
  <p class="lead">Here's what actually happened, so you don't have to learn it the same way I did.</p>
</div>

<ol class="timeline">
  <li>
    <span class="when">Day 1</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="h3">The school felt huge</h2>
      <p>I had a timetable in my hand and no idea which hallway was which. I went up the wrong stairs and was almost late to class. By Friday I knew the way. Everyone figures it out fast.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="when">Week 1</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="h3">Nobody reminds you anymore</h2>
      <p>In elementary school I could kind of get by without a study routine. In Grade 9, nobody reminds you about homework. I didn't notice that right away.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="when">Weeks 4 and 5</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="h3">Everything landed at once</h2>
      <p>The first round of tests and assignments all came in the same couple of weeks. I was scrambling. I stayed up too late, forgot a due date, and felt behind in everything.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="turning-point">
    <span class="when">Week 6</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="h3">I got a calendar</h2>
      <p>I wrote every test, practice and due date in it. I broke big assignments into small pieces and gave each piece a day. It sounds simple, but my head felt a lot lighter once it was all written down.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<section class="short-version">
  <h2>What I'd tell myself in Grade 8</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Start the calendar on day one, not after the first bad week.</li>
    <li>Study a little every night instead of a lot the night before.</li>
    <li>Ask the teacher when you're confused. It's not a big deal.</li>
  </ul>
  <a class="btn" href="/goals">Set your own goals</a>
</section>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
